[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2579095123","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101274#issuecomment-2579095123","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101274","id":2579095123,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Zud5T","user":{"login":"timothyqiu","id":372476,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MjQ3Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/372476?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu","html_url":"https://github.com/timothyqiu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-09T03:12:37Z","updated_at":"2025-01-09T03:19:19Z","body":"JSON does not distinguish between floats and ints, so whether there is a trailing .0 does not matter.\n\nInstead, it is a useful hint that could be picked up by a (third-party) deserializer.\n\nPython also does something like this:\n\n```pycon\n>>> json.dumps({'A':1, 'B':1.0})\n'{\"A\": 1, \"B\": 1.0}'\n>>> data = json.loads('{\"A\": 1, \"B\": 1.0}')\n>>> type(data['A']), type(data['B'])\n(<class 'int'>, <class 'float'>)\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2579095123/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2583649797","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101274#issuecomment-2583649797","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101274","id":2583649797,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Z_14F","user":{"login":"gofastlily","id":120291200,"node_id":"U_kgDOByt_gA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/120291200?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gofastlily","html_url":"https://github.com/gofastlily","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gofastlily/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gofastlily/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gofastlily/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gofastlily/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gofastlily/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gofastlily/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gofastlily/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gofastlily/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gofastlily/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-10T19:08:52Z","updated_at":"2025-01-10T19:08:52Z","body":"TL;DR: I think we can just save work here by not changing how things currently operate.  If anything documentation could be updated to explain to the user what's going on.\n\n---\n\nIs this something that actually needs to be changed?  It seems like a good thing to me, given that at least some third-party deserializers support parsing ints and floats even if they're not part of the JSON spec.\n\n> As of PR https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/47502, floats are always printed with a trailing .0. This is great for most situations, but should not happen with JSON files.\n\nHaving the trailing `.0` doesn't break the JSON spec, so Godot is still rendering valid JSON.\n\n> JSON does not distinguish floats and ints, so the .0 is possibly informative of the number's original type in Godot, but is not necessary for the JSON data, and may be misleading users into thinking that JSON supports floats and ints\n\nIt doesn't seem to me that teaching the end-user about how JSON supports integers and floats is within scope for Godot.  Maybe a note in the documentation would be more helpful as we can provide further context there.\n\nThis just seems like unnecessary work.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2583649797/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2583764514","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101274#issuecomment-2583764514","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101274","id":2583764514,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aAR4i","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","recei